BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exocapitalism and the Superdark Factory – Seminar with Marek Pol
 iks and Roberto Alonso Trillo — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+02:00":20261016T160000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+02:00":20261017T000000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:fded4b76840a5aecb79824e8e1be@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:Exocapitalism is the idea that capitalism doesn't belong to us
 : that it works as a form\, almost like an algorithm\, and could keep work
 ing without us. The seminar runs through several of its core mechanisms 
 – Lift and Fold – before turning to the concept of the Superdark Facto
 ry. Lift is capital's tendency to pull away from fixed costs\, from the gr
 ound\, from the sphere of human affairs. You can see it in an airline that
  no longer sells seats but positions in a queue\, or in a telecom operator
  that sells its towers and keeps using them as a tenant. Fold is the proce
 ss by which difference emerges without any change to the substrate – the
  lens through which we read the software economy. We close \nCategory: Mul
 tidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedu
 le/exocapitalism-and-superdark-factory-seminar-marek-poliks-and-roberto-al
 onso-trillo
LOCATION:Nave 17. Aulario\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/exocapitalism-and-superdark
 -factory-seminar-marek-poliks-and-roberto-alonso-trillo
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
