DESCRIPTION:Designed as a participatory experience that fosters community
 \, shared learning\, and social reflection\, this gathering offers a sanct
 uary of care\, warmth\, and coexistence through a traditional practice rei
 nterpreted through a contemporary lens. Programme Preview MORNING SESSION:
  Crochet and Knitting Workshops (11:00 AM – 2:00 PM) Simultaneous worksh
 ops tailored for various skill levels and ages. Registration: Advance regi
 stration via the Matadero Madrid website. Tickets are €3 per person. Rec
 ommended Age: Intergenerational\, for ages 6 and up. All participants—bo
 th children and adults—must purchase a ticket. Minors must be accompanie
 d by a responsible adult at all times. AFTERNOON SESSION: Kni\nCategory: M
 ultidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/sche
 dule/tejiendo-y-punto
